	var promise = Parse.Promise.as();

	// Comenzamos la importacion

	promise.then(function() {
		// Guardar todos los expositores
		var innerPromise = Parse.Promise.as();

		_.each(expositores, function(expositor){
			innerPromise = innerPromise.then(function(){
				return expositor.save().then(function(){
					console.log('Expositor Guardado');
				});
			});
		});

		return innerPromise;
	}).then(function(){
		// Guardar todos los temas

		var innerPromise = Parse.Promise.as();

		_.each(temas, function(tema){
			innerPromise = innerPromise.then(function(){
				return tema.save().then(function(){
					console.log('Tema Guardado');
				});
			});
		});

		return innerPromise;

	}).then(function(){
		// Asociar temas a expositor

		var innerPromise = Parse.Promise.as();

		_.each(expositores, function(expositor){
			var nombre = expositor.get('nombre');
			var temas = temasParaExpositor[nombre];

			expositor.set('temas', temas);

			innerPromise = innerPromise.then(function(){
				return expositor.save().then(function(){

					console.log('Temas asociados a Expositor');

					var innerPromise2 = Parse.Promise.as();

					_.each(temas, function(tema){
						tema.set('expositor', expositor);

						innerPromise2 = innerPromise2.then(function(){
							return tema.save().then(function(){
								console.log('Expositor Asociado a Tema');
							});
						});
					});

					return innerPromise2;
				});
			});
		});

		return innerPromise;

	}).then(function(){
		console.log('Todo OK');
	}, function(error){
		console.error(error.message);
	});
}
// Fin del Script de Importar
```

## Conclusions

Parse.com is a great help for building applications and prototypes quickly, without the headaches associated with server maintenance and scaling. However, as with everything, the range of needs of a complex application may mean using external services that complement what Parse offers. The following points should be taken into account when considering Parse.com for a new project:

- Parse has a limit of 1 Million Requests in the free version; a popular application can easily exceed it, and one must be prepared to pay the costs of the excess, or to move to the professional or enterprise version if necessary.

- Currently, although it is in the process of being implemented, there is no direct way to move an application from the development environment to a production environment. To do this, the information must be transferred from one application to a new one, but there is no way to transfer the ACLs. A possible solution is to use the JavaScript import.

- Analytics data can be exported, but only manually. There is no API to access that data automatically (yet). External services that fulfill the Analytics role could be [Count.ly](http://count.ly/), [Piwik](http://piwik.org/) and [Google Analytics](http://www.google.com/analytics/)

- The CodeCloud code will be overwritten when it is uploaded; it is recommended to use Git when more than one person works on that code.

- If Javascript is used to create the web version of an application, the access keys will be available; it is important to create ACLs that restrict access to the data.

- Since Parse.com was acquired by Facebook, there is a greater chance that an application that uses Parse will be bought by Facebook if it becomes popular :) .

